{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To determine how many values of \\( x \\) satisfy \\(\\sin x = -0.31\\) within the interval \\(0^\\circ \\le x < 990^\\circ\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the general solutions for \\(\\sin x = -0.31\\):**\n   The sine function is negative in the third and fourth quadrants. The reference angle \\(\\theta\\) for \\(\\sin x = 0.31\\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\theta = \\sin^{-1}(0.31)\n   \\]\n   Using a calculator, we find:\n   \\[\n   \\theta \\approx 18.02^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n2. **Find the angles in the third and fourth quadrants:**\n   - In the third quadrant, the angle is:\n     \\[\n     180^\\circ + \\theta = 180^\\circ + 18.02^\\circ = 198.02^\\circ\n     \\]\n   - In the fourth quadrant, the angle is:\n     \\[\n     360^\\circ - \\theta = 360^\\circ - 18.02^\\circ = 341.98^\\circ\n     \\]\n\n3. **Determine the periodicity of the sine function:**\n   The sine function has a period of \\(360^\\circ\\). Therefore, the general solutions for \\(\\sin x = -0.31\\) are:\n   \\[\n   x = 198.02^\\circ + 360^\\circ k \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x = 341.98^\\circ + 360^\\circ k\n   \\]\n   where \\(k\\) is an integer.\n\n","prefix_end":1063,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,8253,1246,1657,2750,315,17767,856,1124,8,26553,1124,11520,15940,856,284,481,15,13,18,16,57758,2878,279,9873,17767,15,24884,43298,1124,273,856,366,220,24,24,15,24884,43298,59,701,582,686,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,3070,28301,1437,279,4586,9904,369,1124,11520,15940,856,284,481,15,13,18,16,59,1648,1019,256,576,57668,729,374,8225,304,279,4843,323,11737,29136,1783,13,576,5785,9210,1124,11520,15976,57758,369,1124,11520,15940,856,284,220,15,13,18,16,57758,374,2661,553,510,256,1124,9640,256,1124,15976,284,1124,15940,87210,16,25547,15,13,18,16,340,256,1124,921,256,12091,264,29952,11,582,1477,510,256,1124,9640,256,1124,15976,1124,48053